GHOST (physical sheet, principal branch, hbar*a0=1e-3, m=1):
  K(z)=mu_fw(sqrt z) propagator has EXACTLY ONE pole at w*=-1.0005 ~ -m^2,
  N'(w*)=+0.99975, residue ~ +1  (IDENTICAL to healthy KG residue +1).
  Off-axis complex-pole scan over Re,Im in [-3,3]: NONE.
  => branch-cut form factor is GHOST-FREE (one healthy pole, no wrong-sign pole,
     no tachyon). The finite truncation K=1+c z, by contrast, has a SECOND pole
     with residue -a0 hbar/sqrt(...) < 0 = Ostrogradsky GHOST. Nonlocality kills it.
